# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rowan — environment configuration example
#
# Usage:
#   cp .env.example .env.local      # local development
#
# `.env.local` and every other `.env*` file except this one are git-ignored.
# Never commit real credentials, and never paste a production value into this file.
#
# Phase 2 adds the database and authentication variables. All of them are optional
# at build time: Rowan builds, lints, type checks, and starts with an empty
# environment, and each server module reports the absence of the value it needs at
# the moment it is used. Give the shell nothing and it renders the signed-out state.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Public origin of the deployment, used to build absolute URLs (metadata, email links).
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are embedded in the browser bundle: never put a secret here.
# Optional — when unset, metadata falls back to relative URLs and auth redirects are
# derived from the request origin (correct for localhost and preview deployments).
#
#   Local development : http://localhost:3000
#   Preview           : the preview deployment URL Vercel assigns
#   Production        : https://your-production-domain
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://rowan.example.com

# Minimum level emitted by the server-side structured logger.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One of: debug | info | warn | error. Defaults to "info".
# Server-only; it is never sent to the browser.
#
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# PostgreSQL connection string — the database that stores accounts and, in later
# phases, conversations, prompts, and usage records.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-only. A connection string contains a password: never prefix it with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_, never print it, and never commit it.
#
# Required by every database-backed surface. Without it the shell still renders, and
# each data operation fails with a clear "database is not configured" error.
#
# Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → Database → Connection string → URI.
# Use the pooled connection string for serverless deployments and append
# `?sslmode=require` for hosted databases:
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@<host>:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
#
# Local development and the integration suite can point at any PostgreSQL — an
# embedded cluster started by the tests needs no configuration at all:
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/rowan

# Supabase project URL — used for authentication only.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rowan uses Supabase for identity (registration, sign-in, verification, password
# reset) and talks to PostgreSQL directly for data. Server-only, as only the server
# authenticates.
#
# Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API → Project URL.
#
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co

# Supabase anonymous (publishable) key.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Safe by Supabase's own design, but still server-only here: the browser never talks
# to Supabase directly in Rowan, so no key needs to reach it. Rowan's schema grants
# the `anon` role nothing, so this key cannot read a single row of user data.
#
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_...

# Supabase service-role key — the administrative key.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bypasses row-level security and may administer users. Rowan uses it in exactly one
# place: permanently deleting a provider account when the user deletes their Rowan
# account. It is never used for reads, never used for ordinary writes, and never
# sent to the browser.
#
# Store it in your hosting platform's secret store with the narrowest scope available.
# Rotating it immediately invalidates the old value everywhere.
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=sb_secret_...

# Test database for the integration suite (optional, CI and local overrides).
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# When unset, `pnpm test:integration` starts a throwaway PostgreSQL cluster from the
# bundled binaries and applies every migration to it. Set this to use an existing
# database instead (CI service container, local PostgreSQL) — the suite drops and
# recreates the `public` schema in it, so never point it at a database you care about.
#
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/rowan_test
